From eb89278d7c312d236703e39b90d865b44397ec10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:29:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: keep a drained Borg from diving regardless of prior
 direction

"Do not dive when drained" read if (g && BI_ISFIXEXP), but g is only
non-zero at that point when an earlier branch already decided to head
up, so the check never applied to a Borg that had not yet chosen a
direction -- a drained Borg was still free to power-dive. The
sibling "do not dive when full of items" check was translated from the
original dive-cancellation to an unconditional try_not_to_descend;
this one kept the dead g gate.

Apply the drained check unconditionally: a drained Borg no longer
takes the power-dive branches and instead falls through to the
remaining leave-level decisions (heading up when unprepared, restock,
and so on).

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#235.

(cherry picked from commit 6d909bf5216c1e6c5ed199595d9ed3e5baf4b0d8)
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index e4687edc6..35d082d91 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -730,8 +730,12 @@ bool borg_leave_level(bool bored)
     if (sellable_item_count >= 12)
         try_not_to_descend = true;
 
-    /* Do not dive when drained */
-    if (g && borg.trait[BI_ISFIXEXP])
+    /* Do not dive when drained.  This applies whenever the experience is
+     * drained, not only when an earlier check already chose to head up:
+     * the original borg cancelled a decided dive here (g = 0), and the
+     * sibling "full of items" check was translated to an unconditional
+     * try_not_to_descend while this one kept the dead g gate. */
+    if (borg.trait[BI_ISFIXEXP])
         try_not_to_descend = true;
 
     /* Rise a level if bored and unable to dive. */
